      ":question/id": "f44d9ca6-d6e9-5638-a0a7-a7d697b009d5",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\cos x$?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The graph intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1.$\n- **II.** The function is zero at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}.$\n- **III.** The function is zero at $x=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\cos x$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186176047/assets/cosine.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. At $x=0$, the function has value $\\cos 0=1$.\n\n- Statement II is true. $\\cos(\\frac{\\pi}{2})=0$.\n\n- Statement III is true. $\\cos(\\frac{3\\pi}{2})=0$.",
